# core/data/talk/grammar/en/cool_dismiss.tlk - more replies to DISMISS and THREATEN (owner: TK;
# T5b package T5B-COOL). Brush-offs, sulks, sarcasm and cartoon threats: a duck, a postcard, a
# nap, never real harm and never aimed at a child (a child speaker gets a cute deflection).
# No register word. Syntax: core/tools/talkc_gen.py.

# ---- DISMISS -> COMPLAIN -------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.dismiss.c_complain act: complain
  "Hey, don't brush me off! I was in the middle of being interesting."
  "Rude! You can't just wave a hand at people. It's not allowed."
  "Wow, okay. Do I have a sign on my back? Kick me, please?"
  "Fine, ignore me. I'll just sit here and sulk quietly. Loudly."
  "That's cold. My soup is warmer than you. And it's day-old."
  "Oh, I see how it is. Shoved off like a stale biscuit."
  "You could at least pretend to care. Stage whisper it. Anything."
  "I'm not nothing! I'm a whole something! With a hat!"
  "Ugh, that stings. I'll be in the corner. Making a face."
  "Charming. Truly. I'll tell everyone how kind you were."
@rule core.dismiss.c_complain_sad guard: mood=sad act: complain
  "Oh, right. Okay. I'll just go and be sad somewhere else."
  "That hurt a bit. I'm already low. Please don't shove."
@rule core.dismiss.c_complain_angry guard: mood=angry act: complain
  "Don't you dare wave me off! I'm FUMING! Stand still and listen!"
  "Oh, don't give me that. I'm cross enough as it is."
@rule core.dismiss.c_complain_polite guard: polite act: complain
  "Well, that was hardly civil. I only asked for a moment of your time."
  "I do think you might have been kinder, dear. But there we are."
@rule core.dismiss.c_complain_elder guard: elder act: complain
  "Young people. No respect. In my day, you'd be given a stern look."
  "Well! I've been dismissed by better. And worse, to be honest."
@rule core.dismiss.c_complain_flat guard: flat act: complain
  "Wow. {.}Dismissed. I'll put my crying in the diary for later."
  "Rude. {.}I'm offended on the inside. It's quiet in there."
@rule core.dismiss.c_complain_kid guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: complain
  "That's not nice! You have to listen! It's the rule!"
  "Hey! Don't wave at me like that! I'm a person, a small one!"
  "Hmph! You're not listening! Listen to me, please!"

# ---- DISMISS -> DISMISS / TEASE / JOKE / LAUGH ---------------------------------------------------
@rule core.dismiss.c_dismiss tags: gentle act: dismiss
  "Oh, you're dismissing ME? That's adorable. I dismiss you right back." guard: !kid_present
  "Shoo, then. Back to your corner. I'll be fine, with a snack." guard: !kid_present
  "Fine. I'll dismiss you harder, see? Look at the effort."
  "I don't need you. I've got a whole lamp for this." guard: !kid_present
  "Whatever you say. I'm the one with the better lunch."
  "Right, cool, go. Do your little thing. It's fine." guard: !kid_present
  "Your approval means nothing. And I'd like that in writing." guard: !kid_present
  "Bye, then. Don't let the door hit your ego on the way out." guard: !kid_present
@rule core.dismiss.c_dismiss_blunt guard: blunt&!kid_present act: dismiss
  "Good. Because I'd already stopped listening. Several minutes ago."
  "Go on, go. I'll write you a tiny note. It'll say 'no'."
@rule core.dismiss.c_dismiss_quirky guard: quirky tags: gentle act: dismiss
  "Dismissed! By the Order of the Lemon! Please leave by a window."
  "I summon my invisible bodyguard! He's right behind you! Boo!"
@rule core.dismiss.c_dismiss_serious guard: serious&!kid_present act: dismiss
  "As you wish. I shall consider this conversation closed."
  "Very well. I'll file your dismissal under 'ignored'."
@rule core.dismiss.c_tease tags: gentle act: tease
  "Ooh, touchy. Did I step on your invisible tail?"
  "Aww, is someone cranky? Did they skip their biscuit?" guard: !kid_present
  "Look at you, being all brisk. Do you practise that in the mirror?" guard: !kid_present
  "Okay, Your Majesty. I'll curtsy when I'm done with my snack."
  "Sure. Wave your little hand. I'll file you under 'busy'." guard: !kid_present
  "That wave was very elegant. Do it again, I'll score it."
@rule core.dismiss.c_tease_friend guard: rel=friend tags: gentle act: tease
  "Oh, you're grumpy. I'll bring you a snack. And a hat."
  "Fine, fine. You're the boss. Of nothing, but still."
@rule core.dismiss.c_joke act: joke
  "That's okay. I'm used to being ignored. I'm a houseplant at heart."
  "Dismissed? I've been dismissed from better places. A chapel, a bank."
  "Fair enough. I'll go whisper my secrets to the toaster."
  "No problem. I'll go and be fascinating elsewhere."
  "Ouch. Right in the feelings. Good thing I've got spares."
  "Mm. I'd be offended, but I'm busy being a legend."
@rule core.dismiss.c_laugh act: laugh
  "Ha, fair. I'd dismiss me too. I'm a lot."
  "Hah, okay, okay! You got me. That was a smooth brush-off."
  "Ha ha, oof! Right in the dignity. Respect."
  "Pfft, I walked right into that one. Well played."

# ---- THREATEN -> LAUGH / JOKE ----------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.threaten.c_laugh act: laugh
  "Ha, oh no, what will you do? Glare at me? Write a limerick?"
  "Hahaha! You're adorable when you're fierce. Like an angry muffin."
  "Ooh, I'm shaking. Look, my hat is trembling. It's the wind."
  "That's your scary voice? Do it again. I want it as a ringtone."
  "Heh, bold. A threat. And you're holding a spatula."
  "Hee, I'm so scared. I've gone all goosebumpy. Are those goosebumps?"
  "Oh, you big softie. You couldn't scare a mouse. A very sleepy mouse."
  "Ha, go on, then. Release the pigeons. I dare you."
@rule core.threaten.c_laugh_loud guard: loud act: laugh
  "HA, YOU AND WHAT CREW?! A CREW OF SPOONS?! BRING IT!"
  "OOH, I'M SO SCARED! LOOK AT ME! I'M HIDING BEHIND NOTHING!"
@rule core.threaten.c_laugh_flat guard: flat act: laugh
  "Ha. {.}That was my terrified laugh. It sounds the same."
  "Oh no, {.}Fear. Look at my face. It's doing nothing, in fear."
@rule core.threaten.c_laugh_elder guard: elder act: laugh
  "Ha! I've been threatened by tax collectors. You don't scare me, pet."
  "Oh, bless. Go on, I've got my walking stick. It's very pointy."
@rule core.threaten.c_laugh_kid guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: laugh
  "Hee hee, you're not scary! You're funny! Do it again!"
  "Hahaha! You're being silly! Your scary face is wiggly!"
@rule core.threaten.c_joke act: joke
  "Is that a threat or a poem? I can't tell. It rhymed."
  "I'd be scared, but my diary says I'm busy on that day."
  "Threats, eh? I'll add it to my collection. I've got a nice shelf."
  "You'll have to take a number. I've got a queue of threats."
  "Pencil me in for the scary bit. Right after my nap."
  "Ooh, a threat! Did you write it on a card? I'll frame it."
  "My therapist says I shouldn't take threats personally. So, thanks."
  "Please do. I've always wanted a dramatic sequel."
@rule core.threaten.c_joke_quirky guard: quirky act: joke
  "I'll tell the moon, and the moon will tell the owl. You're done."
  "Threaten away! My mood ring is purple. That means 'bring it'."
@rule core.threaten.c_joke_polite guard: polite act: joke
  "How very forceful. Might I suggest a nice cup of tea first?"
  "I do admire your confidence. Do sit down, dear. Have a scone."

# ---- THREATEN -> DISMISS / THREATEN / COMPLAIN -------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.threaten.c_dismiss tags: gentle act: dismiss
  "Please. I've been threatened by cats with more menace." guard: !kid_present
  "Yawn. Was that your best? I've heard scarier from a kettle." guard: !kid_present
  "Sure, sure. Come back when you've got a plan. Or a hat." guard: !kid_present
  "Threaten away. I'll be napping. Ring first."
  "Scary. Truly. Now, if you'll excuse me, I've got soup."
  "I've seen a demon sneeze on a cake. You don't rate." guard: !kid_present
  "Mm-hm. Put it in the suggestion box. Under 'no'." guard: !kid_present
  "That was cute. Next time, add thunder. I love thunder."
@rule core.threaten.c_dismiss_blunt guard: blunt&!kid_present act: dismiss
  "Do it, then. Or shut up. I'm hungry and you're slow."
  "You're all talk, and not even good talk. Move."
@rule core.threaten.c_dismiss_serious guard: serious&!kid_present act: dismiss
  "I see. Do try to keep it within the town's noise limits."
  "Noted. Please submit your threat in triplicate."
@rule core.threaten.c_dismiss_easy guard: easygoing tags: gentle act: dismiss
  "Yeah, whatever. Do your worst. I'm going to lie down."
  "Chill, mate. It's too sunny to be scary today."
@rule core.threaten.c_threaten guard: !kid_present act: threaten
  "Is that so? Well, I'll see your threat and raise you a worse one."
  "Oh yeah? I'll sit on your hat! And I'll stay there!"
  "Try it. I've got a stern look and I'm not afraid to use it."
  "One more step and I'll make a very disappointed face."
  "Watch it. I know a goblin. He owes me a sock."
  "You'll regret that. I'll tell the Mayor. He'll nod slowly."
  "Fine. But I've got a rubber duck and I'm not afraid of it."
  "Say it again and I'll glare. For ten full seconds. Without blinking."
@rule core.threaten.c_threaten_loud guard: loud&!kid_present act: threaten
  "I'LL SHOUT AT YOU! RIGHT NOW! AND THEN AGAIN LATER!"
  "COME AT ME! I'LL BOOP YOU ON THE NOSE! HARD, WITH A CUSHION!"
@rule core.threaten.c_threaten_quirky guard: quirky&!kid_present act: threaten
  "I'll turn you into a teapot! Only for a day! You'll hate it!"
  "I'll hex your socks! They'll slide off at a bad moment!"
@rule core.threaten.c_threaten_rival guard: rel=rival&!kid_present act: threaten
  "Try me. You've been itching for it, so scratch."
  "Oh, we're going there? Good. I've waited all season."
@rule core.threaten.c_complain act: complain
  "That's not nice! Threatening people is rude. And scary, a bit."
  "Hey, no threats in the house. It's a rule. I made it just now."
  "Don't say that! You're making my stomach do the wobbly thing."
  "Ow, my nerves! Please, no threats before lunch."
  "I don't like that. Can we go back to being friends?"
  "You're being scary, stop it! I'll tell the Patrol! They've got whistles!"
@rule core.threaten.c_complain_scared guard: mood=scared act: complain
  "Please don't. I'm already shaking. Even my hair's shaking."
  "Eep, don't! I scare easily! I got scared by my own shadow today!"
@rule core.threaten.c_complain_kid guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: complain
  "That's not fair! I'm telling the grown-ups! Right now!"
  "Stop it! I don't like it! Let's play a nice game instead?"
  "No threats! The Patrol says no threats! Rule number one!"
